    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Dunmore Kell</strong> is a night porter lodging in room 207. He is tired, underpaid and not malicious. He named a dead rat 'S. Rattus, Custodian (Acting)' so that an amended warehouse door in the Lower market would let him wheel unlisted small bones through at night.</p><p><strong>GM notes (Quest 1, 'The Rat on the Door Plate').</strong> Insight or Persuasion <strong>DC 12</strong> gets a full confession. He is a <em>petty offender</em>, not the note-leaver: he uses the door and a bone cart (wheels and boots, never tubes). If asked about the tubes: <em>'The tubes aren't mine. Something clunks down that old terminal at the same hour every night. I don't go near it.'</em> That clears him and points at the real lead (6.4). Fix options: Stellan's Trace Rune / Countermark with Quill (DC 11), a paper fix with Pringus, or report him (lenient).</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
      "alignment": "neutral",
